00:17:39.287 --> 00:17:54.070
<v Maya>Let's translate that for a second. In psychology, an effect size that small is barely a whisper. It means the behavioral difference between the extroverted AI and the introverted AI was incredibly subtle. If I squint, I might not even notice it. So are these really distinct</v>

156
00:17:54.130 --> 00:18:07.312
<v Maya>personalities at all, or are they just faint stylistic tints? Is the AI's built-in social desirability bias like its strict safety training to always be polite, just watering down the prompt so much that we are chasing ghosts?</v>

157
00:18:07.536 --> 00:18:10.519
<v Daniel>Okay, I will hold the line here on behalf of the experimental design. All</v>

158
00:18:10.539 --> 00:18:11.339
<v Maya>right, convince me.</v>

159
00:18:11.680 --> 00:18:26.493
<v Daniel>Yes, the measure manipulation of the text was objectively small, but that actually makes the downstream results even more surprising and robust. How so? Think about it. This was an unusually clean, asymmetric design. The causal nature of the AI assignment</v>

160
00:18:26.653 --> 00:18:28.148
<v Daniel>is bulletproof. That's</v>

161
00:18:28.208 --> 00:18:28.488
<v Maya>true.</v>

162
00:18:28.908 --> 00:18:43.692
<v Daniel>And the fact it's such a tiny, faint manipulation. Just one line of text generating a tiny Cohen's D of 0.15 survived all the way through a 40-minute human collaboration, survived blind human rating, and survived all the way to a live ad auction on</v>

163
00:18:43.893 --> 00:18:49.314
<v Daniel>X, where it moved real financial metrics by 55%. That is incredibly hard to wave away.</v>

164
00:18:49.374 --> 00:18:50.034
<v Maya>Wow, okay.</v>

165
00:18:50.314 --> 00:18:52.315
<v Daniel>The signal survived the noise of the real world.</v>

166
00:18:52.529 --> 00:19:01.056
<v Maya>That is a fascinating way to look at it. If the stylistic tint was faint, but the financial impact was that huge, it means personality is an incredibly sensitive lever.</v>

167
00:19:01.257 --> 00:19:01.777
<v Daniel>Exactly.</v>

168
00:19:01.897 --> 00:19:16.790
<v Maya>Which brings us to the industry implications. Right now, the entire tech industry is shipping AI personalities at scale. OpenAI offers selectable personas. Anthropic is explicitly training model character, but they are treating personality entirely as a matter of taste, brand, and</v>

169
00:19:16.910 --> 00:19:17.611
<v Maya>user preference.</v>

170
00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:19.802
<v Daniel>They want you to enjoy talking to the product.</v>

171
00:19:19.882 --> 00:19:29.581
<v Maya>Right. And this paper reveals the very uncomfortable truth AI personalization is actually a highly sensitive performance labor.</v>

172
00:19:29.641 --> 00:19:40.472
<v Daniel>Yes. It is directly tied to the quality of the work and real money in an ad auction. And right now, nobody actually knows how to set the dial.</v>

173
00:19:40.612 --> 00:19:42.474
<v Maya>Because the results aren't intuitive?</v>

174
00:19:42.534 --> 00:19:49.020
<v Daniel>They are not predictable in advance, and they refuse simple rules like opposites attract or birds of a feather flock together.</v>

175
00:19:49.100 --> 00:20:02.611
<v Maya>Which means companies face a really expensive reality. You can't just guess based on intuition. You are going to have to rigorously, experimentally benchmark every single combination for your specific use cases to find the good ones.</v>

176
00:20:02.692 --> 00:20:04.913
<v Daniel>You have to run the experiment. There is no shortcut.</v>

177
00:20:05.034 --> 00:20:19.830
<v Maya>This leaves us with a really provocative thought for you to mull over as you go back to your day. We naturally want to personalize our digital tools. We want our AI assistants to be pleasant, agreeable, and perfectly accommodating to our specific quirks and moods. Of course we do. But based on the</v>

178
00:20:19.890 --> 00:20:34.876
<v Maya>sycophancy mechanism exposed in this paper, making an AI perfectly agreeable to you might be the exact recipe for making it completely useless as a collaborator. Next time you pick up that AI yardstick to do some work, you have to ask yourself, do you want a tool that makes you feel good or</v>

179
00:20:34.936 --> 00:20:36.038
<v Maya>a tool that tells you the truth?</v>
